# Builder app

The Angular builder (`apps/client`) is **not** a consumer of `@rosettadash/*` runtime packages for its chrome — it uses **`app-*` BEM** and builder-specific components.

## State ownership

- **Single owner:** `BuilderStateService` (signals) — canvas nodes, selection, history
- Components **must not** hold duplicate canvas graph state
- Every user-visible mutator: `recordHistory()` (unless `historySuspended` / `skipHistory`) → immutable `nodes.update` → `markDirty()`
- **No-op guard:** skip history if value unchanged

## Labels

- `ComponentNode.label` — instance rename (canvas/export)
- `ComponentDefinition.label` — catalog name
- Do not collapse these fields

## CSS

- Builder chrome: **`app-*` BEM** (`docs/28-app-component-css-convention.md`)
- Use **`<app-collapsible>`** — never hand-roll accordion markup in builder pages
- Do not copy collapsible CSS into page stylesheets
- Page wrappers: `welcome__*`, `admin-page__*` — not `app-*`

## Preview

- Preview renderers use `data-testid="preview-…"`
- Preview mock data via `@rosettadash/ui-primitives` — not runtime packages for fake rows
- Extension plugins register preview adapters — no hard-coded switch for new palette types

## Palette

- Accordion group headers: `<button>` with `aria-expanded`, Enter/Space support
- Add button test id: `palette-add-{dotted.type}`
- Groups: 2–7 items

## Testing

- Builder interaction changes → `npm run verify:all`
- E2E selectors: `data-testid` only — not CSS classes or visible text

## Must not

- Use `rd-*` classes in builder chrome (preview may render `rd-*` inside preview iframe/host as consumer simulation)
- Commit without verify when touching canvas/inspector/palette

